url: "https://github.com/cloudynirvana/thesis-06-sparse-connectome-controllers"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-21"
abstract: "Relative to lumped adaptive-therapy controllers, do sparse connectome-style policies change closed-loop computational behaviour on a toy cancer ODE in a way that is identifiable from controller architecture alone? Kenyon-cell-style expansion, sparsening, and readout are treated as in-silico controller architecture classes, not as fly-neuron therapy. Adjacent game and visualization repositories are not this paper. Research only. Not a medical device."
keywords:
  - in-silico control
  - adaptive therapy
  - sparse coding
  - Kenyon-cell-style architecture
  - reservoir computing
  - identifiability
  - toy cancer ODE
  - research-only
  - not a medical device
